  "details": "VRCSDK: VRCSDK3-2019.12.21.16.01\nUdonSDK: UDONSDK-2019.12.22.12.32_Public\nSteps of reproduction:\n1. Have a simple cube rotate. My node layout for this example (https://pastebin.com/GTaTGsSR)\n2. Press Play\n3. Stop play once editor is running\n4. open node graph and compile\n5. press play. It should now take longer for the editor to run.\n6. repeat steps 2-5 to increase the time by ~1 second each repetition\nNote: restarting the editor will temporarily reset the time back to what is expected. Repeating steps 2-5 will increase the time again.\nDetails:\nI noticed the more I hit play to test my changes the longer it took to run. Once it hit about 30 seconds I restarted the editor to find the issue fixed, until I started testing more changes and noticed the time get longer again.\nExpected result:\nTesting changes by running the editor then going back to the node graph should not result in a continued increase in time that is not related to graph complexity. In addition making no changes to a graph should not increase the time it takes to run the editor.",
